## Setup

Needs [mise](https://mise.jdx.dev).

```sh
{%- if stack == 'python' %}
mise install      # python, uv, lefthook, cocogitto, jq
mise run install  # git hooks + dependencies
mise run test
mise run lint     # ruff + ty
{%- elif stack == 'typescript' %}
mise install      # bun, lefthook, cocogitto, jq
mise run install  # git hooks + dependencies
mise run test
mise run lint     # biome + tsc
{%- elif stack == 'cpp' %}
mise install      # cmake, ninja, clang-format, clang-tidy, lefthook, cocogitto, jq
mise run install  # git hooks + configure (fetches GoogleTest)
mise run test     # Debug build with sanitizers, then ctest
mise run lint     # clang-format + clang-tidy
{%- else %}
mise install      # lefthook, cocogitto, jq
mise run install  # git hooks
{%- endif %}
```

{% if stack == 'cpp' %}The compiler comes from the system: GCC 13 or Clang 17 or newer, with C++20.

{% endif %}The Claude Code hook in `.claude/settings.json` needs `jq` on `PATH` or in mise's global config (`mise use -g jq`): it reads no project's mise config, so the `jq` above does not serve it.

Commit messages follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org); the `commit-msg` hook checks them with cocogitto.
